matches
Returns true if the pattern matches anywhere in the string.
The pattern need not match the entire string unless its expression requires it.

matches(s, pattern)

matches("123", "[0-9]+")         # true
matches("abc123", "[0-9]+")      # true
matches("abc", "[0-9]+")         # false
matches("hello world", "^hello") # true
===
find
Returns the first match as a shaped value [@match, start, end, text].
start and end are rune indexes into s, so they may be used directly with
string indexing and with the string module.
Returns [@error, :regex, "no match"] if the pattern does not match.

find(s, pattern)

find("abc123def", "[0-9]+")    # [@match, 3, 6, "123"]
find("abcdef", "[0-9]+")       # [@error, :regex, "no match"]
===
find_all
Returns a list of all non-overlapping matches, each as [@match, start, end, text].
Returns [] if the pattern does not match.

find_all(s, pattern)

find_all("a1b2c3", "[0-9]+")   # [[@match, 1, 2, "1"], [@match, 3, 4, "2"], [@match, 5, 6, "3"]]
===
replace
Replaces all matches of the pattern with the replacement string.
Capture groups may be referenced in the replacement as $1, $2, and so forth.

replace(s, pattern, replacement)

replace("a1b2c3", "[0-9]", "X")    # "aXbXcX"
===
replace_first
Replaces only the first match of the pattern.
The replacement is inserted literally; capture references are not expanded.

replace_first(s, pattern, replacement)

replace_first("a1b2c3", "[0-9]", "X")    # "aXb2c3"
===
split
Splits the string at matches of the pattern and returns the parts as a list.

split(s, pattern)

split("a, b, c", ",\\s*")    # ["a", "b", "c"]
